# CasperOS — the storage stack the tablet actually needs in its initramfs.
#
# These are read by mkinitramfs BEFORE the MODULES policy is applied, so they
# are included under `most`, `list` or `dep` alike. Debian's `most` already
# pulls in all of drivers/mmc, so on today's trixie this list is redundancy —
# and it is deliberate redundancy, because it is the difference between "the
# initrd contains mmc_block" and a kernel panic at local_mount_root, and
# 05-finalize.sh checks the built initrd for exactly these names.
#
# Bay Trail's eMMC is an SDHCI controller (PCI id BYT_EMMC / BYT_EMMC2), and on
# some N220/N240 firmware it is enumerated over ACPI instead; iosf_mbi is
# called by both paths on Bay Trail. ext4's crc deps are listed because the
# ramp-up to "root mounts" is the one thing that must never depend on a guess.
ext4
jbd2
crc16
crc32c
mmc_core
mmc_block
sdhci
sdhci_pci
sdhci_acpi
cqhci
iosf_mbi
